    "q-107696": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following is a factor of ${y}^{2}-8y+17?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we let $f(y)={y}^{2}-8y+17.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(y)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-8y+17 & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-8y+{4}^{2})-{4}^{2}+17 & =0 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16+17 & =0 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & ={\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =(\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ y & =4\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our quadratic equation has roots ${y}_{1}=4+\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=4-\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression ${y}^{2}-8y+17$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-8y+17 & =a(y-{y}_{1})(y-{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =(y-(4+\\text{i}))(y-(4-\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, only $y-(4+\\text{i})$ is a factor of ${y}^{2}-8y+17.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-107696-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y-(1-4\\text{i})",
