    "q-177651": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times {2i}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[-0.5,0.5]\\times {1}={(k,1)\\,:\\,k\\in [-0.5,0.5]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(-0.5,1)$ to the point $(0.5,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/6c6aafd9ea78868e953340eaab3862491d275972d690e2ceb27c213dadbcaea6.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times {2i}={(k,2i)\\,:\\,k\\in [-i,i]}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(-i,2i)$ to the point $(i,2i).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/02c8f93a25d7b510d3e238e6d4a974d6ccc2e83f3ac01fe92ce4535fbb4dce48.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/3b3cefa03d71d99e4b7f3b6852ed36512d2a841a37c558034eac5c4b6870799c.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
