    "q-127046": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(2,-5,4)$ and $Q(3,-2,2).$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 3t \\\\ -2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+t \\\\ -5+3t \\\\ 4-2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+t \\\\ y=-5+3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
