    "q-87262": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 52",
      "problem": "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.8,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.5+P(B)-0.4 \\\\ P(B) & =0.8+0.4-0.5 \\\\ P(B) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-87262-a",
